From edaaa6dbfc2d3c5375607a6765aeb1e5276ec114 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "gastown.slit (polecat)" <polecat-gastown.slit@soundit.local>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 23:10:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: transfer prepaid time balance between contracts
 (psa-t8k)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

All prepay operations were previously per-contract, so a client with
leftover prepaid hours on one contract had no way to move them to another
(e.g. consolidating onto a renewal). GitHub #111.

Adds PrepayService::transfer(), which records a matched ledger pair — a
TransferOut debit on the source contract and a TransferIn credit on the
destination — atomically in one DB transaction, with a ContractActivity
logged on each side. The pair deliberately mirrors the existing manual
debit/credit mechanics so the denormalized balance columns stay consistent
with recalculateBalanceLocked(): the transfer-out counts toward the
source's prepay_used, the transfer-in toward the destination's
prepay_total. A from-ledger recalculation reproduces the live state
exactly (asserted in the flagship test), so a transfer can never drift the
balance columns.

Design decisions / constraints honoured:
- Transfers are restricted to two active contracts of the SAME client with
  the SAME tracking unit (hours vs dollars); the balance is conserved.
- Insufficient-balance, same-contract, cross-client, unit-mismatch and
  no-prepay-destination are all rejected (service throws; controller
  surfaces friendly redirects and re-checks defensively).
- The incoming credit inherits the DESTINATION contract's expiry policy via
  expiryForCredit(); the outgoing debit carries no expiry.
- New TransferIn/TransferOut sources are excluded from scopeConsumption so a
  one-time balance movement does not distort the burn-rate / days-until-
  depleted estimate. PrepayExpirationService is unaffected: it replays raw
  signs (not that scope), so a transfer-out correctly draws down source
  lots FIFO and a transfer-in becomes an expirable lot on the destination.

UI: a "Transfer" action + modal on the contract Prepay Balance card, shown
only when the client has another eligible contract. New route
contracts.prepay-transfer.

Validation: new tests/Feature/Prepay/PrepayTransferTest.php (12 cases:
balance movement + ledger-recalc consistency, activity logging, expiry
policy, burn-rate exclusion, every guard, and HTTP happy-path + rejections)
— all green. Full suite 2580 passed / 0 failed on sqlite; Pint clean on all
changed files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
